{"title":"2021 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rectangle A has length 6 cm and area 36 cm<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9add24769580a01164e7c66605736405890bb8ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"17\" />.<br />\nRectangle B has length 12 cm and area 36 cm<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9add24769580a01164e7c66605736405890bb8ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"17\" />.<br />\nRectangle C has length 9 cm and area 36 cm<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9add24769580a01164e7c66605736405890bb8ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"17\" />.<br />\nThe rectangle with the smallest width has a width of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> cm. What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For a rectangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/1754644825336b6708e7fc52bf68e4bf72721bfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w = \\frac{A}{l}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"39\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is the width of the rectangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the area of the rectangle, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> is the length of the rectangle. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/6/7667f92717ccc7852ed2445cd7f169f2851cc72c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/3/9f3767bae98b29edc47e5832c95bb2e9b20432b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/5/595b34e259e022599d24ea4045ec79ffb9d80e48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> be the width of rectangle A, B, and C, respectively. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/2/de25820cbaaf3d5349a44c0a832004aa6a5487e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_{A} = \\frac{36}{6} = 6 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"132\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/4/2f4cc03e64bcf001a5fefdf331cf2ce67cf58c1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_{B} = \\frac{36}{12} = 3 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"133\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62fa35f486fcdbfba65ef6c559847bb70e03cf5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_{C} = \\frac{36}{9} = 4 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"133\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Of these widths, the smallest is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a72aaf4f80f6fb21ba7d6587d520ec9f37b5fea1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed{3 \\text{ cm}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"84\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Without_Finding_All_of_the_Widths.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Without_Finding_All_of_the_Widths)\">Solution 2 (Without Finding All of the Widths)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Without Finding All of the Widths)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in solution 1, we can realize that the width and length of the rectangle are inversely proportional, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/1754644825336b6708e7fc52bf68e4bf72721bfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w = \\frac{A}{l}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"39\" />. Since the rectangles all have the same area as well, this means that the rectangle with the largest length must have the smallest width, which is the rectangle with length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8da2038a882b47e2184ab809431639593cff639b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the width of this rectangle, the width is then:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/7/bd7c36a5e9812dbe3c040c6073b87f512d09f47f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{36}{12} = \\boxed{3 \\text{ cm}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"130\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIMC\" title=\"2021 CIMC\">2021 CIMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Part A Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A 6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Part B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Part B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part B 3</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Intermediate_Competition\" title=\"CEMC Intermediate Competition\">CEMC Intermediate Competition</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017134618\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.021 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.045 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 149/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1246/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 143/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3645/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.332      1 Template:CEMC_CIMC/CSMC_box\n100.00%   15.332      1 -tot